item+ trait src/coordinate_ext.rs :: CoordinateNav :: pub trait CoordinateNav { :: [UPSTREAM] Navigation trait: move forward/backward in a specific dimension. The existing break methods (scroll_break, section_break, etc.) advance AND reset lower dimensions. That's correct for parsing delimiters, but an editor also needs "move to the next book without resetting chapter/section/scroll" for lattice navigation, AND "move backward" which libphext doesn't support at all. `navigate` moves in a dimension, resetting lower dims (like the delimiter does). `peek` moves in a dimension WITHOUT resetting lower dims (for UI preview). :: direct :: api
item+ enum src/coordinate_ext.rs :: Dimension :: pub enum Dimension { :: Dimension enum for editor navigation. Maps 1-9 keys to the nine phext dimensions (scroll=innermost, library=outermost). :: direct :: api
item+ function src/coordinate_ext.rs :: Dimension::delimiter :: pub fn delimiter(&self) -> u8 { :: The delimiter byte for this dimension. :: direct :: api
item+ function src/coordinate_ext.rs :: Dimension::from_index :: pub fn from_index(i: u8) -> Option<Dimension> { :: Convert 1-9 key index to dimension. Returns None for out of range. :: direct :: api
item+ function src/coordinate_ext.rs :: Dimension::name :: pub fn name(&self) -> &'static str { :: Function Dimension::name takes no inputs beyond the value it is called on. It gives back &'static str. :: inferred :: api
