item+ const src/oauth.rs :: CONTENT_SECURITY_POLICY :: pub const CONTENT_SECURITY_POLICY: &str = concat!( "default-src 'self'; ", :: Policy for the embedded editor and the public pages. The shell is one HTML document: an inline script, an inline stylesheet, `onclick` attributes, and `style` attributes. A nonce or a hash does not cover event-handler or style attributes, so those would mean rewriting the shell. `unsafe-inline` stays for that reason. There is no `unsafe-eval`. Sign-in is a same-origin link to `/api/auth/...`, which 302s to Google or GitHub; top-level navigations are not restricted. `upgrade-insecure-requests` is added only when the browser connection is HTTPS, so a local `http://127.0.0.1` session keeps working. :: direct :: api
item+ const src/oauth.rs :: HSTS_VALUE :: pub const HSTS_VALUE: &str = "max-age=31536000"; :: One year. Matches `deploy/nginx-edit.phext.io.conf`. No `includeSubDomains`: this host is `edit.phext.io`, and a future sibling name under that host should not be pinned by accident. :: direct :: api
item~ struct src/oauth.rs :: Limiter :: pub struct Limiter { :: In-memory cap on sign-in attempts per client address, per ten minutes. Counts OAuth start/callback and a bearer token the server rejected (the token box sends that secret as `Authorization` on the next API call). Anonymous 401s are not counted, so opening the signed-out page does not spend the budget. The address is `X-Real-IP` when nginx sets it from `$remote_addr`; otherwise the last `X-Forwarded-For` hop, which is the one a single reverse proxy appends. :: direct :: api
item~ function src/oauth.rs :: Reply::write_to :: pub fn write_to(&self, out: &mut impl std::io::Write) { :: Serialize as an HTTP/1.1 response with `Connection: close`. Auth and session bodies stay `Cache-Control: no-store`. There is no `Access-Control-Allow-Origin`: the editor is same-origin only. :: direct :: api
