item+ function src/media.rs :: is_well_formed_binary_scroll :: pub fn is_well_formed_binary_scroll(stored: &str) -> bool { :: True when `stored` is a well-formed binary scroll: it carries the canonical header and its body is strict base64 (an empty payload — header plus newline, nothing after — is well-formed). A header-prefixed scroll whose body is not strict base64 is malformed: by the format's fetch rule it is text, fetched verbatim, and the text write path may still edit it. Only well-formed binary scrolls are protected from text writes. :: direct :: api
