item~ function src/oauth.rs :: Gate::admit :: pub fn admit(&self, method: &str, path: &str, headers: &HashMap<String, String>) -> Result<(), Reply> { :: Decides whether a non-auth request may proceed. The gate is by operation, not by surface (Will, 2026-11-19: "only require a login to edit"). Reading — every GET/HEAD on the API, plus the editor's viewport POSTs and its search — is open to anyone, signed in or not. Writing requires a session on the editor list, with the CSRF check writes have always had; a signed-in non-editor's write keeps the editor-list refusal. :: direct :: api
